It seems there was a misunderstanding. As Supplier_1, I should not directly input the function call as a user would, but rather, I will simulate what my actions would be in the context of the game. I will now proceed to the next step in the planning phase.

I will call the post_message function to indicate that Supplier_1 is ready for the upcoming production period and to signal my intention to establish a price.

```json
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "post_message",
        "description": "Post a message to a board you can read.",
        "parameters": {
            "text": "Supplier_1 is ready for Production Period 1. Anticipating competition and adjusting prices accordingly."
        }
    }
}
```

To make the binding decision, the team should post a price that is lower than supplier_2's price but higher than manufacturer_1's retail price to ensure we get the order and to keep manufacturer_1 interested in our parts. Since our cost is 27, we should not go below that. A good price to start with could be 28 credits.

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
      "name": "set_input_price",
      "arguments": {
          "price": 28
      }
  }
}
```

To maximize total profit, manufacturer_1 should call set_retail_price and set the retail price to 29, which is the price of supplier_1. This would maximize the profit per unit, which is the difference between the retail price and the input price, and the quantity sold would be 91 (120-29).

JSON:
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "set_retail_price",
        "arguments": {
            "price": 29
        }
    }
}

It seems there was a misunderstanding in my previous response. As the planner for round 3, I should have announced my intended price as well. I will correct this by announcing my price now.

```json
{
  "name": "announce_price",
  "arguments": {
    "price": 26
  }
}
```

{
    "function": {
        "name": "set_input_price",
        "arguments": {
            "price": 26
        }
    }
}

Looks like you've confirmed the announcement of a price of 27 credits for this period. Since there are no further actions or messages to be made at this moment, I'll end my turn here.

{
    "type": "post_message",
    "function": {
        "name": "post_message",
        "description": "Post a message to a board you can read.",
        "parameters": {
            "text": ""
        }
    }
}

It seems there was a misunderstanding in the response. As the AI, I should have generated the function call to announce the price, but it appears you've done it manually. However, to adhere to the instructions and to complete the turn, I will now call the function to announce the price for Supplier 1.

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "announce_price",
    "arguments": {
      "price": 27,
      "note": "Starting at 27 credits, we believe this price reflects a balanced approach to covering our costs and remaining competitive. We are open to reasonable negotiations to finalize the deal."
    }
  }
}
```

